-- title:
--   Rank of the connected Fitting summand equals connected height
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a commutative ring, $p$ a prime such that $p$ is a non-zero-divisor in $\mathcal{O}$, equipped with an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra structure on $\mathbb{Z}/p$ whose structure map has kernel the ideal $(p)$, and assume $\mathcal{O}$ is adically complete for $(p)$. Let $r\in\mathbb{N}$ and let $H_1$ be a Honda system for the element $p$ on $\mathcal{O}^r$: $\mathcal{O}$-linear maps $F,V$ with $F\circ V=V\circ F=p\cdot\mathrm{id}$, together with a submodule $L$ such that every $x\in L$ lying in the range of $F$ is $p\cdot y$ for some $y\in L$, $p\cdot y$ lies in the range of $F$ for $y\in L$, $\operatorname{range}F+L=\mathcal{O}^r$, and $V$ is injective on $L$. Let $G_v$ ($v\in\mathbb{N}$) be finite cocommutative Hopf algebras over $\mathbb{Z}/p$ with coalgebra-algebra maps $s_v:G_{v+1}\to G_v$ that are surjective, with $\dim_{\mathbb{Z}/p}G_v=p^{vr}$, with $\ker s_v$ the ideal generated by the image of the augmentation ideal of $G_{v+1}$ under multiplication by $p^v$, and with the Cartier dual of each $G_v$ a local ring. Let $\pi_v:\mathcal{O}^r\to M(G_v)$ be additive surjections onto the Dieudonné modules $M(G_v)=\mathrm{DieudonneModule}(\mathbb{Z}/p,p,G_v)$ (the direct limit over $n$ of the groups of additive elements of the truncated Witt vectors of length $n$ on $G_v$), with $\pi_v(x)=0$ exactly for $x\in p^v\mathcal{O}^r$, carrying $F$ to Frobenius and $V$ to Verschiebung, and compatible with the transition maps in the sense that the map induced by $s_v$ takes $\pi_{v+1}$ to $\pi_v$. Let $h^c\in\mathbb{N}$ and let $G^c_v$, $G^e_v$ be further families of finite cocommutative Hopf algebras over $\mathbb{Z}/p$, with maps $s^c_v:G^c_{v+1}\to G^c_v$, $q^c_v:G_v\to G^c_v$, $\pi^e_v:G_v\to G^e_v$ and $\Theta_v:G_v\to G^c_v\otimes_{\mathbb{Z}/p}G^e_v$ of coalgebra-algebras, such that each $G^c_v$ is local, each $G^e_v$ reduced, each $s^c_v$ and each $q^c_v$ surjective, $\dim_{\mathbb{Z}/p}G^c_v=p^{vh^c}$, $\ker s^c_v$ the ideal generated by the image of the augmentation ideal under multiplication by $p^v$, each $\Theta_v$ bijective and given by $(q^c_v\otimes\pi^e_v)\circ\mathrm{comul}$, and $q^c_v\circ s_v=s^c_v\circ q^c_{v+1}$. Finally let $M^c,M^{et}$ be complementary submodules of $\mathcal{O}^r$ with $M^c$ free, $M^{et}=\{m:\forall N,\ m\in\operatorname{range}F^N\}$ and $M^c=\{m:\forall k\ \exists N,\ F^Nm\in p^k\mathcal{O}^r\}$. Then $\operatorname{rank}_{\mathcal{O}}M^c=h^c$.
--
--   This is the numerical half of Fontaine's comparison between the Fitting decomposition of a Honda system and the connected–étale splitting of the corresponding $p$-divisible group: the rank of the connected summand is the height of the connected factor. It is used in the construction of split coordinates putting a Honda system into normal form, via [`Deformation.HondaSystem.exists_splitCoordinates_lawful_normalForm`](thm.html#Deformation.HondaSystem.exists_splitCoordinates_lawful_normalForm).
